8698468293", "personaname": "Dr. D", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198698468293/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 6, "playtime_forever": 542, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 542, "last_played": 1783348782, "avatar": "18e873bd0dfadd112edafd65f58ae5033c5e4b2e"}, "language": "english", "review": "I enjoyed Sniper Elite: Resistance overall, especially the large maps, DLC, and Axis Invasion mode. The invasions added tension to the missions, but they happened way too often. Sometimes, as soon as I killed one invading sniper, another invasion would start almost immediately. Some players also played in a really boring way, sitting in one spot and waiting for me to walk through a doorway instead of actually hunting me.\n\nThe story was quite bad, and honestly, I did not follow it nearly as much as I did in Sniper Elite 5, which I enjoyed more. The main character was hard to care about and pretty boring to follow. Most of the missions also felt very similar, so the game started to become repetitive after a while.\n\nThe final mission was especially disappointing. I would barely even call it a mission. You basically just kill a guy while he is escaping on a bike, and when it ended, I was sitting there thinking, “What was even the point of that?”\n\nI still had fun with the gameplay, map sizes, DLC, and Axis Invasions, but the weak story, boring main character, repetitive missions, and disappointing ending held the game back.", "timestamp_created": 1783450340, "timestamp_updated": 1783450340, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1738246187", "hardware": {"system_ram": "65313", "os": "Windows 11", "cpu_name": "13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K", "adapter_description": "NVIDIA 